*PPD-Adobe: "4.3"
*%
*% myshare - generic PDF passthrough queue, shared by the "CloudToRaspi"
*% and "CloudWeb" queues (only the queue name decides which display
*% target is served, see deploy/nextcloud-backend-wrapper.sh). Same
*% technique as cups-pdf: cupsFilter2 declares application/pdf as the
*% final format, so CUPS stops the filter chain after PDF generation and
*% passes the finished PDF directly to the backend (no rasterizing needed).
*%
*FormatVersion: "4.3"
*FileVersion: "1.0"
*LanguageVersion: English
*LanguageEncoding: ISOLatin1
*PCFileName: "PRNTQRV.PPD"
*Manufacturer: "Generic"
*Product: "(myshare)"
*ModelName: "myshare"
*ShortNickName: "myshare"
*NickName: "Generic myshare PDF-Passthrough"
*PSVersion: "(3010.000) 0"
*LanguageLevel: "3"
*ColorDevice: True
*DefaultColorSpace: RGB
*FileSystem: False
*Throughput: "1"
*LandscapeOrientation: Plus90
*TTRasterizer: Type42
*cupsVersion: 2.0
*cupsManualCopies: True
*cupsFilter2: "application/pdf application/pdf 0 -"

*OpenUI *PageSize/Media Size: PickOne
*OrderDependency: 10 AnySetup *PageSize
*DefaultPageSize: A4
*PageSize A4/A4: "<</PageSize[595 842]/ImagingBBox null>>setpagedevice"
*PageSize Letter/Letter: "<</PageSize[612 792]/ImagingBBox null>>setpagedevice"
*CloseUI: *PageSize

*OpenUI *PageRegion/Media Size: PickOne
*OrderDependency: 10 AnySetup *PageRegion
*DefaultPageRegion: A4
*PageRegion A4/A4: "<</PageSize[595 842]/ImagingBBox null>>setpagedevice"
*PageRegion Letter/Letter: "<</PageSize[612 792]/ImagingBBox null>>setpagedevice"
*CloseUI: *PageRegion

*% Deliberately NOT borderless (ImageableArea == PaperDimension): CUPS
*% automatically generates a "_borderless" media variant for that, which
*% GTK print dialogs (e.g. Firefox) sometimes can't resolve ("Unknown
*% paper size iso_a4_210x297mm_borderless") - the dialog then aborts
*% without ever sending the job to CUPS (lp/LibreOffice aren't affected,
*% since they bypass the GTK paper size resolution).
*DefaultImageableArea: A4
*ImageableArea A4/A4: "18 18 577 824"
*ImageableArea Letter/Letter: "18 18 594 774"

*DefaultPaperDimension: A4
*PaperDimension A4/A4: "595 842"
*PaperDimension Letter/Letter: "612 792"
